## Phased Implementation

### Phase 1 — Create global module (no call-site changes)

| Task | Deliverable |
|------|-------------|
| Create `src/types/index.ts` | All Tier-1 types copied from current sources |
| Unify `Point` | Single primitive; document mapping from `Vec`/`Pt` |
| Document sections | Comment blocks per domain in one file |

**Tier 1 (must move first):** `Point`, `SpinType`, `EnglishType`, `AimState`, `ChargeDir`, `Lang`, `GameMode`, `Settings`, `Marble`, `BoardDimensions`, AI public types.

### Phase 2 — Rewire imports (game + context)

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `game/physics.ts` | `Vec` → `Point`; export `Marble` type from `src/types` only (physics imports type) |
| `game/boardLayout.ts` | import `BoardDimensions` from `src/types` |
| `context/SettingsContext.tsx` | import `Settings`, `Lang`, `AiLevel` from `src/types`; export `Settings` from types only |
| `game/ai/*.ts` | import `Point`, AI types from `src/types`; delete `game/ai/types.ts` |
| `game/ai/index.ts` | re-export AI types from `src/types` (backward compat) or point consumers to `src/types` |
| `i18n.ts` | import `Lang` from `src/types`; export `Lang` re-export from types |

### Phase 3 — Rewire imports (views + utils)

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `BilliardsView.tsx` | Remove inline `SpinType`/`EnglishType`; use `BilliardsTurn` |
| `FourBallView.tsx` | same + `FourBallTurn` |
| `TrajectoryLine.tsx`, `MagnifierOverlay.tsx` | shared `AimState`, `ChargeDir` |
| `IntroScreen.tsx` | `GameMode` from `src/types` |
| `App.tsx` | import `GameMode` from `src/types` |
| `SettingsScreen.tsx` | `AiLevel` from `src/types` |

### Phase 4 — Cleanup

| Task | Done when |
|------|-----------|
| Delete `game/ai/types.ts` | all imports use `src/types` |
| Remove `Vec` / `Pt` aliases | grep empty |
| `Settings.language` typed as `Lang` | no inline `'ko' \| 'en'` |
| Optional: `TranslationKey` | `t(lang, key: TranslationKey)` — stricter i18n |
| Optional: `tsconfig` path `@/types` | cleaner imports |

### Phase 5 — Guardrails (ongoing)

- New cross-module union/interface → add to `src/types/index.ts` first.
- Module-private planner/UI props → stay in module.
- No runtime exports in `src/types` (types only; `import type` enforced where possible).
- Consider ESLint `no-restricted-imports` blocking new exports of domain types from old paths.

---

## Naming Decisions (resolve before coding)

| Question | Recommendation |
|----------|----------------|
| `Vec` vs `Pt` vs `Point` | **`Point`** — neutral, used by physics + AI + overlays |
| One file vs `src/types/*.ts` | **One file** for now (~40–80 lines of types); split only if file exceeds ~200 lines |
| Export `Settings` from context or types? | **`src/types` only**; context imports it |
| `Wall` in global? | **Only if** geometry stays AI-private — keep in `geometry.ts` if no external imports |
| Component `Props` in global? | **No** unless shared by 2+ components (future `GameViewBaseProps`) |

